0,Makalero - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Makalero,"Makalero or Maklere is a Papuan language spoken in the Lautém district of East Timor. It was previously considered to be a dialect of Makasae, but is nowadays seen as a separate language, both by its speakers and linguists.",Makalero,Trans-New Guinea
1,Music of Papua New Guinea - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Papua_New_Guinea,"The music of Papua New Guinea encompasses a wide range of traditional and contemporary styles developed across the country's highly diverse ethnic groups. Traditional celebrations known as sing-sing feature communal song and dance, and form a central part of cultural life.",Makalero,Trans-New Guinea
2,Trans–New Guinea languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trans–New_Guinea_languages,"Trans–New Guinea is an extensive family of Papuan languages spoken on the island of New Guinea and neighboring islands, a region corresponding to the country Papua New Guinea as well as parts of Indonesia.",Makalero,Trans-New Guinea
